{
  "id": "claude-rig-pilot-20261007",
  "scope": "Owner-commissioned deterministic-rig pilot for Roshan's wave with LTX animation as the motion guide, run as two tests at the owner's request. LTX Union take 1 is tracked (numbers only) and solved onto one fixed-length rig. Run 1 deliberately ignores the whole-frame, whole-sprite, no-Roshan-rig and written-handoff rules (owner-permitted test): a standalone Godot 4.7.2 Skeleton2D rig with skinned approved parts, rendered and measured. Run 2 restores the rules: proportion-locked structural guides (W3 lengths, one master phase) for the next whole-frame LTX take, plus an untested controlled-comparison runner. No game file, runtime path or finding lifecycle changes. Revision 2 of run 1 (owner review 2026-10-07, ODR-RIG-PILOT-REV2-20261007): the LTX arm path is smoothed, whole-body acting, underwater idle, hair flow and a pilot-only painted blink are authored on the LTX timing, and rig edge artifacts are repaired. Revision 3 (owner rejected revision 2: overdraw, figure not moving as a whole, rough crops; ODR-RIG-PILOT-REV2-REJECTED-20261007): run 1 is closed as evidence. Under \"Continue, trial methods until satisfied\" (ODR-RIG-PILOT-TRIALS-20261007) the run-2 takes run on the owner's RTX 3060 Ti through a PC job runner (ComfyUI graphs only, input hashes, node allow-list, 8-take cap counting failures) fed through the connected folder; jobs a1 (rig guides only) and a2 (plus frame-40 lock and finger sentence) are queued. Because the owner made outfit compatibility critical (ODR-RIG-PILOT-COSMETICS-20261007), whole-frame clips now flow into the game's outfit system: clip_cells.py maps take frames to 256 px cells, clip_pose_fit.py writes a constant-size, bodice-tracked pose fit, and tools/build_fashion_outfits.gd gains an opt-in --fit/--out mode that bakes ribbon, party, garden and disguise onto any clip atlas (default game outputs byte-identical). Proven on Union take 1 frames.",
