  "acceptance_gaps": "Run 1 is closed: the owner rejected revision 2 (overdraw, figure not moving as a whole, rough crops), and as a rules-off test it was never eligible for production under ODR-SPRITE-WHOLE-UNIT-20261007 and ODR-ROSHAN-WHOLE-FRAME-20261005. Run 2's LTX takes, their measure_wave reports and owner review are outstanding; the PC runner is untested until the owner starts it. The outfit clips are reference-only (no runtime atlas, FashionDesigner.SOURCES entry or pose_fit.json change); owner art review of outfits in motion, the garment's whole-pixel slip (<= 0.5 px) and non-rotation are open. Mobile renderer, device, child and runtime gates are outstanding. MA-ROSHAN-006 and MA-VIS-008 lifecycles are unchanged.",
  "lessons": [
    {
      "lesson": "A fixed-length rig solved from LTX footage holds Roshan's size exactly (figure 0.05%, head 0.16%) and is cheap, but as runtime art it reintroduces part layers and an arm that moves alone; use it to author proportion-locked guides, not as the delivered sprite.",
      "write_back": "assets_src/cinematics/claude_rig_pilot_20261007/README.md#run-1-rules-off-runtime-rig-in-godot-472",
      "recurrence_key": "roshan-size-drift"
    },
    {
      "lesson": "Measure the guide family before generating: the Union take-1 guides themselves asked for the forearm to change from -62% to +41% of the contract, and the take followed them.",
      "write_back": "assets_src/cinematics/claude_rig_pilot_20261007/data/run2_measure.json",
      "recurrence_key": "roshan-size-drift"
    },
    {
      "lesson": "When rendering Godot animations frame by frame, set the AnimationPlayer to manual callback mode before seeking; a paused player still advances during the frame and shifts every capture.",
      "write_back": "assets_src/cinematics/claude_rig_pilot_20261007/run1_godot/tools/render_frames.gd",
      "recurrence_key": "godot-frame-capture"
    },
    {
      "lesson": "Do not copy noise-level body motion or per-frame solves from generated footage onto a rig: smooth the LTX path (weighted by fit confidence) and author secondary motion on its timing, or the rig reads as frozen and jittery at once.",
      "write_back": "assets_src/cinematics/claude_rig_pilot_20261007/scripts/animate_rev2.py",
      "recurrence_key": "rig-motion-quality"
    },
    {
      "lesson": "Overlay parts cut from one drawing must exclude neighbouring materials (hair in a sleeve overlay) and joint pivots must sit inside the covering part, or skinned motion exposes cuts and blobs.",
      "write_back": "assets_src/cinematics/claude_rig_pilot_20261007/scripts/build_parts.py",
      "recurrence_key": "rig-motion-quality"
    },
    {
      "lesson": "A cut-out or skinned rig cannot meet whole-sprite acting: overlapping parts overdraw, each part turns about its own pivot, and moving a limb uncovers pixels the drawing never had. Keep rigs for guides and measurement.",
      "write_back": "assets_src/cinematics/claude_rig_pilot_20261007/README.md#run-1-revision-2-whole-body-blink-hair-owner-review-2026-10-07",
      "recurrence_key": "rig-motion-quality"
    },
    {
      "lesson": "Animation clips get outfits through the same per-cell builder as static atlases, but the bodice box must keep one size and only move with the tracked bodice; per-cell measured boxes would make clothing breathe.",
      "write_back": "assets_src/cinematics/claude_rig_pilot_20261007/README.md#cosmetics-the-game-outfits-on-an-animation-clip",
      "recurrence_key": "outfits-on-animation"
    }
